<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taleh</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Taleex</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taleh (Taleex) is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sool">Sool</a> region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a>, the main stronghold of the Dervish state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammed-abdullah-hassan">Mohammed Abdullah Hassan</a>. From 1913 the Dervishes built there a complex of massive stone forts and towers. In early 1920 British aircraft bombed them in one of the first uses of air power in a colonial war, and the ground forces that followed ended the Dervish state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taleh.jpg" alt="Taleh" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Scoobycentric · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Taleh_Castle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
